  "statement": "If a product of the four ell=5 composite generators lies in <E> and no proper prefix does, its <E>-exponent is 1 (the single generator E), 2 (the single generator E^2), or even.",
  "what_this_means": "(LEMMA) is FALSE as a free-monoid statement -- there are first-return words of length 7 with an ODD <E>-exponent, so the O*-step alphabet is not a pure group fact and cannot be proved without legality constraints. But (LEMMA) IS proved, as an exact group computation, for every first-return word of length <= 6. Consequently a bound of 6 on the number of preparation macro-edges between two consecutive O* visits would close the alphabet lemma, and with it the winding argument and the parity. That is exactly the long-standing open 'small preparation-depth bound' item: it is now known to be sufficient, not merely desirable."
